  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade unions in Trinidad and Tobago are facing significant challenges in collective bargaining negotiations within the public sector. The ratification of Convention 151 can help address these issues. The ILO will support trade unions in initiating discussions on the ratification of C 151, including conducting gap analyses, reviewing legislative provisions related to essential services in line with International Labour Standards (ILS), and assessing the general institutional framework for essential services.

Additionally, the ILO will focus on enhancing trade union reporting on Article 22 of the ILO Constitution to strengthen their position on the implementation of ILO conventions. In the context of ongoing labour law reform, the ILO will assist trade unions in identifying major gaps from their perspective and making suggestions based on best regional and global practices. This collaboration aims to benefit trade unions by improving their negotiation capabilities and ensuring compliance with international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
